-   entry .monad   derives `Monad[F]` for any type with a single `flatMap` method and a `Functor[F]`
-       An `inline given` macro, in implicit scope. `#bind` calls the type's own `flatMap`, and
-       `point` and mapping come from the `Functor` it finds. A missing `Functor` is a compile
-       error, _could not find Functor value for `Play`_ (↯/s.17.5); a type with no `flatMap` is
-       another, _the type `Play` has no flatMap methods_ (↯/s.17.1), and one with several overloads
-       of `flatMap` a third, _the type `Play` has more than one possible flatMap method_ (↯/s.17.3).
-   entry #bind   applies a container-returning function to a container's contents, and flattens
-       `monad.bind(value)(lambda)`: `flatMap` by another name.
-   entry #flatMap   the extension form of `#bind`, so that `for`-comprehensions work through a `Monad`
-       Usable on an `F[value]` wherever this `Monad[F]` is in lexical scope as a value.
+   entry .monad   deriva `Monad[F]` para cualquier tipo con un único método `flatMap` y un `Functor[F]`
+       Una macro `inline given`, en el ámbito implícito. `#bind` llama al propio `flatMap` del
+       tipo, y `point` y la transformación vienen del `Functor` que encuentra. Que falte el
+       `Functor` es un error de compilación, _could not find Functor value for `Play`_
+       (↯/s.17.5); un tipo sin `flatMap` es otro, _the type `Play` has no flatMap methods_
+       (↯/s.17.1), y uno con varias sobrecargas de `flatMap` un tercero, _the type `Play` has
+       more than one possible flatMap method_ (↯/s.17.3).
+   entry #bind   aplica una función que devuelve un contenedor al contenido de un contenedor, y aplana
+       `monad.bind(value)(lambda)`: `flatMap` con otro nombre.
+   entry #flatMap   la forma de extensión de `#bind`, para que las comprensiones `for` funcionen a través de una `Monad`
+       Se puede usar sobre un `F[value]` siempre que esta `Monad[F]` esté en el ámbito léxico
+       como valor.

- entry .Cofunctor   a typeclass mapping a function backwards into a contravariant container: `contramap`
+ entry .Cofunctor   una clase de tipos que aplica una función hacia atrás en un contenedor contravariante: `contramap`

= entry .Cofunctor   a typeclass mapping a function backwards into a contravariant container: `contramap`
-   detail
+   detail

-       `Cofunctor[F]` is the dual of `Functor` for a contravariant `F[-value]`, such as a
-       consumer, an encoder or an ordering: given a function `value2 => value`, it turns an
-       `F[value]` into an `F[value2]` by adapting its input. Unlike the other three typeclasses,
-       it has no derivation: an instance is written by hand.
+       `Cofunctor[F]` es el dual de `Functor` para un `F[-value]` contravariante, como un
+       consumidor, un codificador o una ordenación: dada una función `value2 => value`, convierte
+       un `F[value]` en un `F[value2]` adaptando su entrada. A diferencia de las otras tres
+       clases de tipos, no tiene derivación: una instancia se escribe a mano.

=       it has no derivation: an instance is written by hand.
=
-       ```scala
+       ```scala

=       it has no derivation: an instance is written by hand.
=
=       ```scala
-       import soundness.*
+       import soundness.*

-       trait Sink[-value]:
+       trait Sink[-value]:

-         def accept(value: value): Unit
+         def accept(value: value): Unit

-       given Cofunctor[Sink]:
+       given Cofunctor[Sink]:

-         def apply[value, value2](sink: Sink[value])(lambda: value2 => value): Sink[value2] =
+         def apply[value, value2](sink: Sink[value])(lambda: value2 => value): Sink[value2] =

-           value2 => sink.accept(lambda(value2))
+           value2 => sink.accept(lambda(value2))

=           value2 => sink.accept(lambda(value2))
-       ```
+       ```

=       ```
